x86_64-linux  clang emits only the C2 variant of a constructor it writes for a class - here P's implicit move constructor - where cxx1 emits C1 and C2, the difference implicit-move.nonames records: an implicit constructor is inline by nature and has no out-of-line form. C1 and C2 are identical for a class with no virtual bases and both are mergeable, so it costs object size and nothing else.
